{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-275347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{3},0,-2⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨-\\sqrt{3},10,-10⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\sqrt{3},10,-10⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{3})\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =3+0+20 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-275347" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275347" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-73457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a=⟨1,-3,2⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-1,-1⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,-3,0⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-73457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-3))i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 3)j+(2\\cdot (-3)-(-1)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-3i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,-3,-3⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-73457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-73457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b