te" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-128091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-128091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{8})(\\sqrt{8})+(4)(-1)+(-3)(2) \\\\  & =-8-4-6 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-317303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317303" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $a=⟨1,2,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,0,-2⟩,$ and $c=⟨0,-2,1⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2))i-((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))j+((-1)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-4i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-4,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4+2+6 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-275348" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-275348" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,-1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =1\\,(1)\\,-\\,2\\,(22)\\,+\\,3\\,(-4) \\\\  & =1-44-12 \\\\  & =-55.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-317315" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-317315" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-55"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,-1,2⟩$, $b=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $c=⟨2,4,2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 3)+2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-12-2+16 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-20054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-128107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,9,3⟩,$ $b=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-128107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-9(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)+3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =0-27+15 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/state.json" "file_sha256" "436608b4e551d4d9f7ccbcbb13f947280b5c70e3e2dea9ab49252754b462ddb2"} {"question" "q-128107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fae40cd04e4e1c69e8a0e56e457e0e2bc2a1d4d365105fc1daf64e5b26622205"} {"question" "q-128107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/